---
const faqs = [
  {
    q: "How do I know if I need a jump-start or a replacement?",
    a: "If the car starts after a jump but the battery seems weak again within a day or two, or it's more than three to four years old, that usually points to replacement rather than repeated jump-starts.",
  },
  {
    q: "Can a car battery be replaced at my location?",
    a: "In most cases, yes — mobile battery replacement is common and doesn't usually require a workshop visit. Some vehicles need the replacement battery registered to the car's electrical system, which can affect how it's done.",
  },
  {
    q: "How long do car batteries typically last in Dubai conditions?",
    a: "Sustained high heat is hard on lead-acid batteries and tends to shorten their working life. Many batteries in the UAE need replacing sooner than their manufacturer-rated lifespan would suggest elsewhere.",
  },
  {
    q: "What is an AGM battery?",
    a: "Absorbent Glass Mat — a sealed, vibration-resistant battery design that handles deep cycling and higher electrical loads well. Manufacturers typically specify AGM for more demanding stop-start and energy-recuperation systems, or where electrical loads are higher.",
  },
  {
    q: "What is an EFB battery?",
    a: "Enhanced Flooded Battery — a step up from a conventional flooded battery in cycling durability, commonly fitted as standard in entry-level stop-start vehicles.",
  },
  {
    q: "Why does my car battery keep dying?",
    a: "Common causes include a parasitic drain (something drawing power while the car is off), a failing alternator not fully recharging the battery, frequent short trips, or a battery that's simply reached end of life.",
  },
  {
    q: "Can a weak alternator look like a battery problem?",
    a: "Yes — the symptoms overlap a lot. A battery that tests fine but keeps going flat is a common sign the alternator, not the battery, is the actual issue.",
  },
  {
    q: "Do some modern cars require battery registration?",
    a: "Yes. A number of newer vehicles — commonly German makes with battery management systems — need the replacement battery registered or coded to the car's electronics after installation.",
  },
  {
    q: "How do I identify the correct battery for my car?",
    a: "The existing battery's label is usually the best starting point — it typically shows group size, capacity (Ah) and cold-cranking amps, along with the correct chemistry. Not every owner's manual lists the same detail, so fitment should ultimately be confirmed against a reliable vehicle- or manufacturer-specific fitment guide rather than assumed from the manual alone.",
  },
];
---

<section class="faq" id="faq">
  <div class="container faq-inner">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <h2>Battery questions, answered clearly.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-list">
      {
        faqs.map((faq) => (
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>
              <span>{faq.q}</span>
              <svg class="faq-chevron" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="M4 6.5L8 10.5L12 6.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" />
              </svg>
            </summary>
            <p>{faq.a}</p>
          </details>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .faq {
    padding-block: var(--section-space);
    background: var(--bg-soft);
  }

  .faq-inner .section-heading {
    max-width: 34rem;
    margin-bottom: clamp(2rem, 1.6rem + 1.6vw, 3rem);
  }

  .faq-list {
    max-width: 44rem;
  }

  .faq-item {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-medium);
  }

  .faq-item summary {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding-block: 1.25rem;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .faq-item summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  .faq-chevron {
    width: 18px;
    height: 18px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    transition: transform var(--dur-standard) var(--ease-standard);
  }

  .faq-item[open] .faq-chevron {
    transform: rotate(180deg);
  }

  .faq-item p {
    padding-bottom: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: var(--fs-body);
    line-height: var(--lh-body);
    max-width: 40rem;
  }

  .faq-item summary:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--focus-ring);
    outline-offset: 4px;
    border-radius: 4px;
  }
</style>
